		<div class="texto-blog">					
		<p>In this article we will see how to create a <strong>RESTful API in CodeIgniter 4</strong>, with the use of <strong>API Response Trait</strong>, something new that is incorporated in this new version, we will also learn how to use routes and the use of routes of type <strong>resource</strong>.</p>

		<h2>How to create a RestFul api codeigniter 4?</h2>

		{{ include('inc/ad_defect.html.twig') }} 	
		
		<p>First we will start from our controller, this is in <code>nameApp/app/Controller/Users.php</code>, we are going to make a <strong>api rest of type CRUD</strong> to perform operations with users.</p>

		<pre class="text-code">
		<code>
		// import the trait
		use CodeIgniter\API\ResponseTrait;

		// import the model
		use App\Models\UserModel;

		class Users extends BaseController
		{
			// use the trait
			use ResponseTrait;

			// we declare the variables
			protected $UserModel;			

			protected $validation;	


			public function __construct()
			{

				$this->UserModel = new UserModel();

				// load the helper form
				helper('form');				

				// load the validation service
				$this->validation =  \Config\Services::validation();

			}

			public function index()
			{				
				
				// query, it would be select * from users;
				$data['users'] = $this->UserModel->findAll();			

				// we pass the data to him, and we get a code 200
				return $this->respond($data);			
				
				
			}


			public function create()
			{
				// We declare validation rules from the front-end
				$rules = [
					'first_name' => [
						'rules'  => 'required',
						'errors' => [
							'required' => 'Name is required.'
						]
					],
					'last_name' => [
						'rules'  => 'required',
						'errors' => [
							'required' => 'LastName is required.'
						]
					],
					'password' => [
						'rules'  => 'required',
						'errors' => [
							'required' => 'Password is required.'
						]
					],
					'email'    => [
						'rules'  => 'required|valid_email',
						'errors' => [
							'required' => 'Email is required.',
							'valid_email' => 'Verify the email.'
						]
					],
				];		

				// we get everything we send by the method post
				$data = $this->request->getPost();

				

				// if validation fails
				if (!$this->validate($rules)) {

					$errors = $this->validator->listErrors();			

					return $this->failValidationError($errors);					
					
				}else{

					// query to create a resource, insert into users etc
					$data = $this->UserModel->save($data);

					// method when creating a resource status code 201
					return $this->respondCreated($data);
				}		
				
			}


			public function show($id)
			{
				

				if (!$data = $this->UserModel->find($id)) {			

					
					// we use a default exception of the framework, to status code 404
					throw \CodeIgniter\Exceptions\PageNotFoundException::forPageNotFound("Un error a ocurrido");
					

				}else{

					// status code 200
					return $this->respond($data);
				}
				
				
			}

			public function update($id)
			{
				
				// we get everything we send by methods put o patch
				$data = $this->request->getRawInput();
				

				if (!$user = $this->UserModel->find($id)) {

					// method when we can't find a resource
					return $this->failNotFound('User with  id nro:'.$id.' no found.');
					
				}else{

					// update users etc
					$data['user'] = $this->UserModel->update($id,$data);

					return $this->respond($data);


				}

				
				
			}


			public function delete($id)
			{		

				
				// We validate that we delete a user by id, delete users etc
				if ($data = $this->UserModel->delete($id)) {			

					// response when delete
					return $this->respondDeleted();
					
				}
				
				
			}

			

		}
		</code>
		</pre>

		<h2>How do routes work in codeigniter 4?</h2>

		<p>Now we go with the routes, the routes are in <code>nameApp/app/Config/Routes.php</code>, we create a resource type route <strong>resource</strong>, remember to disable the method <code>setAutoRoute(false)</code>, since if we leave it in true we can enter with <strong>class name / controller name</strong>.</p>

		<div class="text-center">

		<img class="img-fluid" src="../assets/img/ci4_rest.png" alt="ci4_test">

		</div>

		<p>Now we are going to list the routes associated with our controller <strong>users</strong>, which is the name of the class that we are passing.</p>


		<pre class="text-code">
		<code>
	php spark routes
		</code>
		</pre>

		<p>And in this way we would list all the routes associated with our controller methods and each of the <strong>endpoints</strong>, where we can use tools like postman, to test apis in the format <strong>json</strong> or any other.</p>

